from pathlib import Path
import html, json, re
OUT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
ROOT=OUT.parents[1]
REPO='https://github.com/lupuszr/neural-commons'
D=ROOT/'docs/validation-agnews'
s=json.loads((D/'summary.json').read_text())
e=json.loads((D/'heldout-output.json').read_text())
a,b=s['base_accuracy']*100,s['candidate_accuracy']*100
TITLE='An AI agent improved another LLM by editing 2,268 weights. DKG checked the result.'
SUBTITLE=f'News classification rose from {a:.1f}% to {b:.1f}% on 1,000 held-out examples. A second local DKG participant reproduced it.'
body=f'''<p>Can an AI agent improve another language model by directly editing its weights?</p>
<p>We now have a concrete, task-specific result in <strong>Neural Commons</strong>: a Codex-controlled agent edited <strong>2,268 BF16 weights</strong> in an unmodified pretrained SmolLM2-135M-Instruct checkpoint. On a fixed 1,000-example AG News test subset, accuracy rose from <strong>{a:.1f}% to {b:.1f}%</strong>. A separate local participant reproduced the result through <a href="https://x.com/origin_trail">@origin_trail</a>’s Decentralized Knowledge Graph.</p>
<p>The inspiration was <a href="https://x.com/rikiyatakehi/status/2117313742891327994">Rikiya Takehi’s post</a> about <a href="https://rikiyat.github.io/blog/weight-space-programming/">Sparks of Weight-Space Programming</a>. This project explores that agent-to-weights idea and the collaboration infrastructure around it. It does not claim to reproduce the paper’s Qwen results.</p>
<p>Code and evidence: <a href="{REPO}">github.com/lupuszr/neural-commons</a>.</p>
<h2>What the agent actually changed</h2>
<p>The recorded controller used <strong>Codex with an existing login</strong>, requesting GPT-6 Astra. An OpenAI Responses API backend is also implemented; its live path has not been validated in this environment.</p>
<p>The host exposed tools to inspect weights, identify tokens, measure development examples and propose numerical edits. For this experiment, edits were restricted to the four task-label embedding rows: World, Sports, Business and Technology. These embeddings are tied to the model’s output weights.</p>
<p>The agent tested 13 proposals using 128 labeled development examples. It used supervised activation contrasts: differences between class means of the base model’s hidden states. The agent chose the coefficients and hypotheses; the host applied the recorded arithmetic. <strong>No gradients or optimizer were used.</strong> This still uses labeled data, and the contrast tool is an engineered affordance—not a claim that the agent invented the entire method unaided.</p>
<figure><img src="assets/07-weight-agent-proposal.png" alt="Actual application proposal showing the Codex controller and 2,268 changed BF16 weights."><figcaption>Actual Neural Commons proposal: a recorded agent decision becomes a reproducible weight patch.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>A real held-out improvement</h2>
<p>A separate 256-example validation split selected the candidate under a fixed rule. Then the checkpoint was frozen before the 1,000-example final test. The prompt, dataset split, original model and acceptance policy were fixed before the search.</p>
<p>The final result: <strong>{round(a*10)}/1,000 → {round(b*10)}/1,000 correct</strong>, a gain of <strong>{b-a:.1f} percentage points</strong>. Label negative log-likelihood fell from <strong>{s['base_label_nll']:.3f} to {s['candidate_label_nll']:.3f}</strong>. The patch corrected {s['corrected']} errors and introduced {s['regressed']} new ones.</p>
<figure><img src="assets/09-weight-results.png" alt="Measured held-out AG News accuracy before and after the agent weight edit."><figcaption>Measured accuracy on the fixed 1,000-example AG News test subset. The agent did not receive these examples.</figcaption></figure>
<p>The acceptance contract also required preserving a previously exposed 56-example sentiment guard. Its accuracy and NLL stayed unchanged. A supplementary local check preserved the original scores on all 872 previously exposed SST-2 examples too. These checks constrain the claim; they do not establish that every capability was preserved.</p>
<figure><img src="assets/06-weight-evaluation.png" alt="Actual evaluation marked passed, with original and candidate news accuracy."><figcaption>The frozen candidate passed the news-improvement policy and the mandatory sentiment guard.</figcaption></figure>
<h2>Why use OriginTrail DKG?</h2>
<p>A screenshot of an improved score is a claim. Other participants need the exact model, patch, inputs, evaluator and policy to check it.</p>
<p>Neural Commons links <strong>ModelVersion, Hypothesis, PatchProposal, Evaluation, Review and DerivedVersion</strong> records in a DKG Context Graph. Content hashes bind the checkpoint, tokenizer, configuration, dataset, controller transcript and acceptance policy.</p>
<ol><li><strong>Propose:</strong> the agent freezes an edit; the generic Rust engine creates and reconstructs its patch.</li><li><strong>Share:</strong> DKG carries the linked experiment records and referenced artifacts to a participant starting with an empty artifact store.</li><li><strong>Reproduce:</strong> that participant verifies hashes, reconstructs the checkpoint and runs its locally configured evaluator.</li><li><strong>Return evidence:</strong> it publishes an evaluation and review through DKG; the first participant checks the author and proposal relationship.</li></ol>
<p>In this run, both participants produced <strong>identical scores and the identical evaluator-output hash</strong>, including the regression guard. They used separate DKG identities, stores and evaluator processes on one physical machine.</p>
<figure><img src="assets/08-weight-dkg-review.png" alt="Actual DKG readback of the second participant's matching successful evaluation."><figcaption>The second participant’s evaluation, retrieved through DKG. This LLM experiment used two local participants.</figcaption></figure>
<p>Weight files use native DKG artifact transport with hashed manifests and bounded blobs; individual weights are not RDF triples. DKG provides peer connectivity, Context Graph authorization and shared provenance. Neural Commons performs tensor edits and evaluation. DKG makes evidence available for checking; it does not make an improvement claim automatically true.</p>
<h2>Failures and boundaries stay in the record</h2>
<p>The first agent edit failed: it increased confidence without improving sentiment accuracy. A later SST-2 edit improved its target task but damaged the older sentiment probe. Both experiments remain documented. That regression motivated the mandatory guard in this news experiment.</p>
<p>The result is four-way forced-choice classification with one fixed plain-text prompt, on a length-filtered test subset. It is not an optimized chat-prompt baseline, a comparison against fine-tuning, or proof of better free-form generation. Public benchmark exposure during pretraining cannot be excluded.</p>
<p>The DKG run uses Shared Working Memory, a disposable local EVM and a documented local compatibility patch. It establishes local reproducibility, not public-chain finality or independent institutional validation. Earlier laptop/Mac mini transport tests are separate; this LLM result has not yet been reproduced across those two physical machines.</p>
<p>The useful next step is to let more agents propose edits, with broader regression checks and independent participants deciding which improvements survive scrutiny. The named-tensor Rust engine remains architecture independent; task adapters are replaceable.</p>
<p>Explore the <a href="{REPO}">repository</a>, <a href="{REPO}/blob/main/docs/AGNEWS-RESULTS.md">measured result and limitations</a>, <a href="{REPO}/blob/main/docs/AGNEWS-WORKFLOW.md">reproduction workflow</a>, and <a href="{REPO}/tree/main/docs/validation-agnews">recorded evidence</a>. Built with <a href="https://x.com/origin_trail">@origin_trail</a> as the shared evidence layer.</p>'''
style='body{max-width:860px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px;font:19px/1.65 Arial;color:#162d30}h1{font-size:44px;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:29px;margin-top:48px}a{color:#14665b}figure{margin:32px 0}img{max-width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid #cad8d5}figcaption{font-size:14px;color:#526c67}.sub{font-size:23px;color:#526c67}'
(OUT/'article.html').write_text(f'<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>{html.escape(TITLE)}</title><style>{style}</style><h1>{TITLE}</h1><p class="sub">{SUBTITLE}</p><img src="assets/01-cover-x.png" alt="Neural Commons weight editing and DKG verification">{body}')
plain=re.sub(r'<figure><img src="([^"]+)" alt="[^"]*"><figcaption>(.*?)</figcaption></figure>',lambda m:'\n\n[INSERT IMAGE: '+m[1]+']\nCaption: '+m[2]+'\n\n',body,flags=re.S)
plain=re.sub(r'<a href="([^"]+)">(.*?)</a>',lambda m:m[2]+' ('+m[1]+')',plain)
plain=plain.replace('<h2>','\n\n').replace('</h2>','\n\n').replace('</p>','\n\n').replace('<li>','\n• ')
(OUT/'article.txt').write_text(TITLE+'\n\n'+SUBTITLE+'\n\n'+html.unescape(re.sub('<[^>]+>','',plain)).strip()+'\n')
(OUT/'source/transfer.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><main>'+re.sub(r'<figure>.*?</figure>','',body,flags=re.S)+'</main>')
base='*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0d1a1e;color:#f0f7f4;font-family:Arial;padding:60px 72px}.eyebrow{font-size:19px;letter-spacing:3px;color:#a1e6ca}h1{font-size:72px;line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-2px;margin:38px 0 24px}.sub{font-size:27px;color:#b5c9c3;line-height:1.4}.footer{position:absolute;bottom:38px;left:72px;right:72px;font-size:18px;color:#9cb6af;display:flex;justify-content:space-between}.mint{color:#a1e6ca}'
cover=f'<div class="eyebrow">NEURAL COMMONS / ORIGINTRAIL DKG</div><h1>2,268 weights edited.<br><span class="mint">A measurable improvement.</span></h1><div class="sub">News classification: {a:.1f}% → {b:.1f}% on 1,000 held-out examples.<br>A second local DKG participant reproduced the result.</div><div class="footer"><span>Codex controller · SmolLM2-135M · No gradients</span><span>github.com/lupuszr/neural-commons</span></div>'
(OUT/'source/cover-x.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>'+base+'body{width:1600px;height:640px;overflow:hidden}</style>'+cover)
chart=f'<div class="eyebrow">ACTUAL WEIGHT-AGENT EXPERIMENT / HELD-OUT RESULT</div><h1 style="font-size:62px">Same model. Same prompt.<br><span class="mint">{b-a:.1f} percentage points more accurate.</span></h1><div class="sub">SmolLM2-135M-Instruct · AG News · fixed 1,000-example test subset</div><div class="rows"><div class="row"><span>Original</span><div class="track"><div class="bar original" style="width:{a}%"></div></div><b>{a:.1f}%</b></div><div class="row"><span>Agent candidate</span><div class="track"><div class="bar" style="width:{b}%"></div></div><b>{b:.1f}%</b></div></div><div class="note">2,268 BF16 weights changed · 56-example sentiment guard unchanged.<br>Two local DKG participants reproduced identical metrics and output hashes.</div><div class="footer"><span>Task-specific forced-choice result; no general capability claim.</span><span>Source: recorded evaluator output</span></div>'
cs='.rows{margin-top:50px}.row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:25px;margin:32px 0}.row>span{width:240px;font-size:27px}.track{width:880px;height:55px;background:#243b3d;border-radius:5px;overflow:hidden}.bar{height:100%;background:#a1e6ca}.original{background:#94aaa4}.row>b{font-size:34px}.note{font-size:24px;line-height:1.5;color:#b5c9c3;margin-top:45px}'
(OUT/'source/weight-results.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><style>'+base+cs+'body{width:1600px;height:900px;overflow:hidden}</style>'+chart)
(OUT/'publishing-notes.txt').write_text('UNPUBLISHED X ARTICLE DRAFT\nEditor: https://x.com/compose/articles/edit/2117595581161832448\nDo not publish without author instruction.\n\n'+TITLE+'\n\nCover: assets/01-cover-x.png\nInline: 07-weight-agent-proposal.png, 09-weight-results.png, 06-weight-evaluation.png, 08-weight-dkg-review.png\nEvidence: docs/validation-agnews. Historical failures retained. Official mention: @origin_trail.\n')
(OUT/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'title':TITLE,'editor':'https://x.com/compose/articles/edit/2117595581161832448','status':'unpublished draft','repository':REPO,'mention':'@origin_trail','evidence':'docs/validation-agnews','images':['01-cover-x.png','07-weight-agent-proposal.png','09-weight-results.png','06-weight-evaluation.png','08-weight-dkg-review.png']},indent=2)+'\n')
print('Prepared article and image sources from recorded evidence.')
